--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party notices
--------------------------------------------------------------------------

1. Statically linked Rust crates

   The `ntfs-mac` binary statically links the Rust crates enumerated in
   `THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md` (generated from `Cargo.lock`). Each entry lists
   the crate version, its SPDX license expression, and its upstream
   repository, so the applicable attribution notices can be reproduced.

   The crate inventory is also available at runtime:

       ntfs-mac license --third-party

2. Externally invoked programs (NOT bundled, NOT linked)

   The following programs are executed as child processes from `PATH` or
   from well-known install locations. No source code from these projects
   is copied into, linked against, or redistributed with ntfs-mac; the
   user installs them separately, and each remains under its own license.

     * ntfs-3g      https://github.com/tuxera/ntfs-3g
                    provides `ntfs-3g`, `mkntfs`, `ntfsfix`, `ntfsclone`
     * macFUSE      https://osxfuse.github.io/
                    kernel/FS extension providing the FUSE layer
     * FUSE-T       https://www.fuse-t.org/
                    alternative userspace FUSE layer for Apple Silicon
     * rsync        https://rsync.samba.org/
                    used by `ntfs-mac copy`
     * diskutil, hdiutil, mount, open, osascript, sw_vers
                    Apple macOS system utilities
     * launchctl    Apple macOS service manager, used by `ntfs-mac daemon`

3. Fonts, icons and other assets

   Any bundled graphical asset is listed in `THIRD_PARTY_LICENSES.md`. The
   QR code shipped for `ntfs-mac sponsor` is generated by the author and is
   covered by the project license.

